From 2200ee86de9ee39d99c69419a1061ecb884cf5ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:53:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] standalone: Program a target from the on-board SPI Flash

Standalone programming: a long press on the user key programs a target
from an image that `bmpflash provision` stored in the probe's on-board
SPI Flash, without a host. `monitor flasher info` lists the stored
image, `monitor flasher write` programs from GDB.

- The image is bmpflash's provisioning format: a 4KiB header ("BMPF",
  CRC32 of the header block, section table) and per section its data.
  The header CRC is checked; the section data carries no checksum.
- Scans SWD, then JTAG, attaches to each target found (many drivers
  only build their Flash map on attach) and programs the first one
  whose Flash holds every section: erases all section ranges first
  (sections can share a sector), writes, verifies by reading back,
  resets and detaches. It does not check that the image was built for
  that chip, as when programming by hand.
- Runs only while no GDB session is attached to a target, and also
  without a host connected (polled from the GDB wait loop). Everything
  talking to the target runs inside TRY/CATCH, with its own target
  controller so driver messages never wait for an absent GDB session.
- The LED blinks fast while programming, stays on for 3s on success,
  and blinks an error code on failure (2 no image, 3 no matching
  target, 4 erase/write failed, 5 verify failed, 6 communication
  error). A log goes to the AUX USB serial port, or to GDB.
- New meson option standalone_support (default off, needs the
  platform's key and LED hooks); enabled for weact-u585, where the key
  is PA0 and the platform's LED macros give way during the blink codes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
